# The table editor, a table made from nothing (tests/t1/pinball3d_editor.sh, criterion 1 of ZN-649.04), window 1440x900: walls, two
# flippers, a plunger lane, three bumpers, a bank of targets, a sound and a mission, then Save and Export.
# The table's name (nothing is selected: the form is the table's own).
4 key f meta
5 text name
6 key Tab
7 text Starter
8 key Enter
# The outer wall: four points round the board, Enter; then the round dot of its top stretch is dragged up until the stretch is a
# half circle (near one, the arc is exactly one).
10 key g meta
11 text +wall
12 key Enter
14 move 508 823
15 down
16 up
17 move 508 301
18 down
19 up
20 move 831 301
21 down
22 up
23 move 831 823
24 down
25 up
26 key Enter
28 move 669 301
29 down
30 move 669 250
31 move 669 139
32 up
# The plunger lane, in one step: its wall, its gate, the plunger.
34 key g meta
35 text +plunger-lane
36 key Enter
# The table's axis goes to the middle of what the lane leaves of the board.
38 move 669 118
39 down
40 move 663 118
41 move 658 118
42 up
# The guide that feeds the left flipper, and its mirror image.
44 key g meta
45 text +wall
46 key Enter
48 move 508 677
49 down
50 up
51 move 590 737
52 down
53 up
54 key Enter
56 key m
# The left flipper, and its mirror image: the right one.
58 key g meta
59 text +left-flipper
60 key Enter
62 move 600 747
63 down
64 up
66 key m
# Three bumpers; the third snaps to the axis.
68 key g meta
69 text +bumper
70 key Enter
72 move 613 387
73 down
74 up
76 key g meta
77 text +bumper
78 key Enter
80 move 702 387
81 down
82 up
84 key g meta
85 text +bumper
86 key Enter
88 move 656 453
89 down
90 up
# A bank of three targets on the left wall: one is placed and made to face the table, then copied twice and each copy moved with
# the arrows (a centimetre a press with Shift).
92 key g meta
93 text +standup-target
94 key Enter
96 move 514 486
97 down
98 up
100 key f meta
101 text angle
102 key Tab
103 text 0
104 key Enter
106 key Escape
108 key d meta
109 key ArrowLeft shift
110 key ArrowLeft shift
111 key ArrowDown shift
112 key ArrowDown shift
114 key d meta
115 key ArrowLeft shift
116 key ArrowLeft shift
117 key ArrowDown shift
118 key ArrowDown shift
# A sound, played by the first bumper when it is hit.
120 key g meta
121 text +sound
122 key Enter
124 key g meta
125 text bumper1
126 key Enter
128 key f meta
129 text sounds.hit
131 move 1300 112
132 down
133 up
135 move 1300 168
136 down
137 up
# Two rules, written as the file has them: the bumpers and the targets score.
139 key g meta
140 text +rule
141 key Enter
143 key j meta
145 key a meta
146 text {"on":"bumpers","event":"hit","do":[{"do":"score","value":500}]}
148 move 420 500
149 down
150 up
152 key g meta
153 text +rule
154 key Enter
156 key j meta
158 key a meta
159 text {"on":"targets","event":"hit","do":[{"do":"score","value":1000}]}
161 move 420 500
162 down
163 up
# A mission: its name, and its step (three hits of the bumpers).
165 key g meta
166 text +mission
167 key Enter
169 key f meta
170 text name
171 key Tab
172 text Warmup
173 key Enter
175 key g meta
176 text rules.missions[0].steps[0]
177 key Enter
179 key j meta
181 key a meta
182 text {"text":"Bumpers","on":"bumpers","event":"hit","count":3}
184 move 420 500
185 down
186 up
# Save, then Export: the table as one file.
188 key s meta
192 key e meta+shift
